-------- User Land  --------- between kernel and user land - syscalls are employed (user vs kernel mode)

# Kernel

Linux kernel contains generic code and drivers and also architecture specific ccode also.

Unix and Linux used the Basic I/O System (BIOS) for bootstrapping itself.

Power ON - Power On Self Test (POST), its part of the BIOS. - basically to make sure all the hardwares are good before booting the OS.

This BIOs setup is now effectively replaced by UEFI - unified Extensible Fireware Interface  defines a software interface between an OS and platform firmware.

