# PROCESS

- A process is a user facing unit, based on an excutable program.

- A thread is a unit of execution in the context of a process/

- Multi threading  - process has a number of parallel executions going on, potentially running on differnt CPUs.

# Sessions
 - Contains one or more process groups and represent a high level user facing unit with optional tty attached. - basically your login to a remote node can be said as session.

 # Process groups
  - Contains one or more process, kernel identifies the process group using Process Group ID(PGID)


